{title: 652 - Love at Home}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #652 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 652}
{meta: category Christian Home - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]There is beauty [Bb]all around,
[F]When there’s love at [C]home;
[F]There is joy in [Bb]every sound,
[F]When there’s [C7]love at [F]home.
[C]Peace and plenty [F]here abide,
[Bb]Smiling fair on [C7]every side;
[F]Time doth softly, [Bb]sweetly glide,
[F]When there’s [C7]love at [F]home.
[Bb]Love at [F]home, love [Dm]at [C]home;
[F]Time doth softly, [Bb]sweetly glide,
[F]When there’s [C7]love at [F]home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[F]Love at home, [Bb]love at home;
[F]Time doth [C]softly, sweetly glide,
[F]When there's [Bb]love at home.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Kindly heaven smiles above, [Bb]When there's love at home;
[F]All the earth is fill'd with [C]love, When there's love at home.
[F]Sweeter sings the brooklet by, [Bb]Brighter beams the azure sky;
[F]O, there's One who [C7]smiles on high When [F]there's love at home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Jesus, make me wholly Thine, [Bb]Then there's love at home;
[F]May Thy sacrifice be mine, [C]Then there's love at home.
[F]Safely from all harm I'll [Bb]rest, With no sinful care distress'd,
[F]Thro' Thy tender [C7]mercy blessed, When [F]there's love at home.
{end_of_verse}
